Kaiyang Zhou, Jingkang Yang, Chen Change Loy, and Ziwei Liu.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">Learning to prompt for vision-language models.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><em id="bib.bib75.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">IJCV</em>, 2022.

</span></li>
    
</ul>
</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Additional Preliminaries</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Latent Diffusion Model and Stable Diffusion</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proposed method utilizes Stable Diffusion (SD) v1.4, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rombach et al., 2022b</a>)</cite>, which is based on Latent Diffusion Models (LDM) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rombach et al., 2022a</a>)</cite>. It performs diffusion within the latent space of an autoencoder, consists of two main components: a diffusion model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dhariwal &amp; Nichol, 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2020</a>)</cite> and a vector quantization autoencoder <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">Van Den Oord et al., 2017</a>)</cite>. The autoencoder is pre-trained to encode an image <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> into spatial latent codes with an encoder (<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\mathcal{E}(I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\mathcal{E}(I)</annotation></semantics></math>) and to reconstruct the image with a decoder (<math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}(\mathcal{E}(I))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}(\mathcal{E}(I))</annotation></semantics></math>). Meanwhile, the diffusion model learns to produce latents that fit within the autoencoder’s latent space. Especially, the objective of the T2I latent diffusion model for a text embedding <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{LDM}}=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{E}(\mathcal{I}),\mathbf{E},\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1),t}\left[\left\|\epsilon-\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t},t,\mathbf{E})\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>LDM</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐄</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{LDM}}=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{E}(\mathcal{I}),\mathbf{E},\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1),t}\left[\left\|\epsilon-\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t},t,\mathbf{E})\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the noisy latent at timestep <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is a sample from normal distribution, and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is the denoising diffusion model parameterized by <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. To encode a text prompt, a text embedding <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E}</annotation></semantics></math> encoded by a text encoder. To construct this structure of model, SD uitilizes a U-Net <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ronneberger et al., 2015</a>)</cite> for the latent diffusion model and a CLIP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Radford et al., 2021</a>)</cite> encoder for the text encoder.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Preliminaries on Previous Concept Erasing Approaches</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We divide recent fine-tuning based methods into two groups: learning based <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gandikota et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and non-learning based <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gandikota et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lu et al., 2024</a>)</cite> approaches.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Learning-based approaches</span>  For erasing target concept, FMN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2023a</a>)</cite> focuses on attention re-steering to minimize attention maps associated with target concepts without significantly deteriorating remaining concepts. It has shown that this intuitive approach can effectively remove harmful or biased contents with flexibility across various concepts and models.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">ESD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gandikota et al., 2023</a>)</cite> is inspired by energy-based composition <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Du et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Du et al., 2021</a>)</cite>.
It aims to decrease the probability of generating an image based on the latent <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>
based on the likelihood of an embedding <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E}_{\text{tar}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mtext>tar</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E}_{\text{tar}}</annotation></semantics></math> for the target concept, which is adjusted by a scaling factor <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{\theta}(x)\propto\frac{P_{\theta^{*}}(x)}{P_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{E}_{\text{tar}}|x)^{\eta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mtext>tar</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>η</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{\theta}(x)\propto\frac{P_{\theta^{*}}(x)}{P_{\theta^{*}}(\mathbf{E}_{\text{tar}}|x)^{\eta}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta^{*}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta^{*}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> represents the distribution generated by the original model. Then, it suggest to update the model with a gradient for <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla\log P_{\theta^{*}}(x)-\eta(\nabla\log P_{\theta^{*}}(x|\mathbf{E}_{\text{tar}})-\nabla\log P_{\theta^{*}}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mtext>tar</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla\log P_{\theta^{*}}(x)-\eta(\nabla\log P_{\theta^{*}}(x|\mathbf{E}_{\text{tar}})-\nabla\log P_{\theta^{*}}(x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Finally, it updates the model <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> by Tweedie’s formula <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Efron, 2011</a>)</cite> for a noisy latent <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t},\mathbf{E}_{\text{tar}},t)\leftarrow\epsilon_{\theta^{*}}(x_{t},t)-\eta\left[\epsilon_{\theta^{*}}(x_{t},\mathbf{E}_{\text{tar}},t)-\epsilon_{\theta^{*}}(x_{t},t)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mtext>tar</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mtext>tar</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\epsilon_{\theta}(x_{t},\mathbf{E}_{\text{tar}},t)\leftarrow\epsilon_{\theta^{*}}(x_{t},t)-\eta\left[\epsilon_{\theta^{*}}(x_{t},\mathbf{E}_{\text{tar}},t)-\epsilon_{\theta^{*}}(x_{t},t)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Especially it empirically verified that updating only CA layers (ESD-x) can effectively erase the target concept while maintaining the remaining concepts relatively well. Meanwhile, fine-tuning all parameters (ESD-u) in the model can holistically erase the image containing the target concept.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Based on ESD, AdvUnlearn <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2024</a>)</cite> proposed a method that is robust to adversarial attacks. Specifically, it seeks to find an embedding <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐄</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> that minimizes the following objective:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{\|\mathbf{E}-\mathbf{E}_{\text{tar}}\|_{0}\leq\rho}\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|\epsilon_{\theta}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{E}\right)-\epsilon_{\theta^{*}}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{E}_{\text{tar}}\right)\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐄</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mtext>tar</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐄</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mtext>tar</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{\|\mathbf{E}-\mathbf{E}_{\text{tar}}\|_{0}\leq\rho}\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|\epsilon_{\theta}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{E}\right)-\epsilon_{\theta^{*}}\left(\mathbf{x}_{t}|\mathbf{E}_{\text{tar}}\right)\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Then, the unlearned model for the target concept is retrained with <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{ESD}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ESD</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{ESD}}</annotation></semantics></math> using the adversarial text embedding. By repeating this process, the unlearned model becomes more robust to attack prompts.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Non-learning based approaches</span>  As non-learning based approaches, UCE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gandikota et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and MACE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lu et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, and RECE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gong et al., 2024</a>)</cite> use a closed-form solution. Briefly, they find the linear projections <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> of keys and values in the cross-attention layers such that:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{W}_{\text{new}}=\text{arg}\min_{\mathbf{W}^{\prime}}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\left\|\mathbf{W}^{\prime}\mathbf{E}_{\text{tar}}^{n}-\mathbf{W}_{\text{old}}\mathbf{E}_{\text{sur}}^{n}\right\|_{F}^{2}+\lambda\sum_{m=1}^{M}\left\|\mathbf{W}^{\prime}\mathbf{E}_{\text{rem}}^{m}-\mathbf{W}_{\text{old}}\mathbf{E}_{\text{rem}}^{m}\right\|_{F}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mtext>new</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>arg</mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mmultiscripts><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mprescripts></mprescripts><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mstyle><mo>⁡</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐄</mi><mtext>tar</mtext><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐄</mi><mtext>sur</mtext><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐄</mi><mtext>rem</mtext><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐄</mi><mtext>rem</mtext><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{W}_{\text{new}}=\text{arg}\min_{\mathbf{W}^{\prime}}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\left\|\mathbf{W}^{\prime}\mathbf{E}_{\text{tar}}^{n}-\mathbf{W}_{\text{old}}\mathbf{E}_{\text{sur}}^{n}\right\|_{F}^{2}+\lambda\sum_{m=1}^{M}\left\|\mathbf{W}^{\prime}\mathbf{E}_{\text{rem}}^{m}-\mathbf{W}_{\text{old}}\mathbf{E}_{\text{rem}}^{m}\right\|_{F}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{\text{old}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{\text{old}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the original key/value projection. The terms in Equation (<a href="#A1.E1" title="In A.2 Preliminaries on Previous Concept Erasing Approaches ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ Concept Pinpoint Eraser for Text-to-image Diffusion Models via Residual Attention Gate" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>) are the erasing and anchoring objective, respectively. It has a closed-form solution and compute <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> directly.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">MACE further ensures the erasure of the target concept by using SAM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kirillov et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, to produce segmentation masks of generated images for the target concept. These masks are used to suppress the attention for each target concept within the CA map of the diffusion model. For training, LoRA modules are inserted in the CA layers of the model for each target concept. Then, the multiple LoRAs are integrated by a loss function, which also propose a term to retain the remaining concepts. This approach effectively prevents forgetting of concepts similar to the target concepts.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">RECE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gong et al., 2024</a>)</cite> basically utilizes the closed-form solution proposed in UCE and enhances robustness against adversarial prompt attacks. RECE repeat to generate an adversarial prompt <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐄</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and erase for the adversarial prompt. For this, it generates the adversarial prompt by solving a closed-form objective for the prompt as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{E}^{\prime}=\text{arg}\min_{\mathbf{E}}\sum_{l}\|\mathbf{W}^{l}_{\text{new}}\mathbf{E}-\mathbf{W}^{l}_{\text{old}}\mathbf{E}_{\text{tar}}\|_{2}^{2}+\lambda\|\mathbf{E}\|_{2}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐄</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>arg</mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>l</mi></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mstyle><mo>⁡</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mtext>new</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐄</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mtext>old</mtext><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mtext>tar</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐄</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{E}^{\prime}=\text{arg}\min_{\mathbf{E}}\sum_{l}\|\mathbf{W}^{l}_{\text{new}}\mathbf{E}-\mathbf{W}^{l}_{\text{old}}\mathbf{E}_{\text{tar}}\|_{2}^{2}+\lambda\|\mathbf{E}\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p">Then, for the attack prompt, <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{\text{old}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{\text{old}}</annotation></semantics></math> in Equation (<a href="#A1.E1" title="In A.2 Preliminaries on Previous Concept Erasing Approaches ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ Concept Pinpoint Eraser for Text-to-image Diffusion Models via Residual Attention Gate" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>) is replaced with <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{\text{new}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mtext>new</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{\text{new}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the weights are recomputed to block the attack prompt. By repeating this process, RECE effectively defends against adversarial prompt attacks. We note that while RECE finds new embeddings from scratch, our approach differs in that we learn residual embeddings to be added to the original target embeddings.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proofs of Theorems</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We will use the notations and definitions in the main paper to prove Theorems 1, 2, and 3.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1a" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1a.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\tilde{W}}_{k}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\tilde{W}}_{k}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\tilde{W}}_{v}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\tilde{W}}_{v}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> be the updated weights of <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{k}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{k}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{v}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{v}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume that <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||\mathbf{E}||_{2}\leq M_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐄</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||\mathbf{E}||_{2}\leq M_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{z}\|_{\infty}\leq M_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{z}\|_{\infty}\leq M_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Denoting the Lipschitz constant of the linear transforms <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐖</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathbf{W}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>𝐖</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathbf{W}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is its spectral norm, the following holds:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\tau(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{E};\mathbf{\tilde{W}}_{k}^{h},\mathbf{\tilde{W}}_{v}^{h})-\tau(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{E};\mathbf{W}_{k}^{h},\mathbf{W}_{v}^{h})\|_{2}\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\left[C_{1}^{h}\|\Delta\mathbf{W}_{k}^{h}\mathbf{E}\|_{F}+C_{2}^{h}\|\Delta\mathbf{W}_{v}^{h}\mathbf{E}\|_{F}\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐄</mi><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐄</mi><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mi>𝐄</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mi>𝐄</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{E};\mathbf{\tilde{W}}_{k}^{h},\mathbf{\tilde{W}}_{v}^{h})-\tau(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{E};\mathbf{W}_{k}^{h},\mathbf{W}_{v}^{h})\|_{2}\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\left[C_{1}^{h}\|\Delta\mathbf{W}_{k}^{h}\mathbf{E}\|_{F}+C_{2}^{h}\|\Delta\mathbf{W}_{v}^{h}\mathbf{E}\|_{F}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{W}=\mathbf{\tilde{W}}-\mathbf{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{W}=\mathbf{\tilde{W}}-\mathbf{W}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}^{h}=\frac{M_{1}M_{2}\sqrt{m-1}}{m\sqrt{m}}L_{\mathbf{W}_{o}^{h}\mathbf{W}_{v}^{h}}L_{\mathbf{W}_{q}^{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}^{h}=\frac{M_{1}M_{2}\sqrt{m-1}}{m\sqrt{m}}L_{\mathbf{W}_{o}^{h}\mathbf{W}_{v}^{h}}L_{\mathbf{W}_{q}^{h}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="Thmtheorem1a.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}^{h}=L_{\mathbf{W}_{o}^{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}^{h}=L_{\mathbf{W}_{o}^{h}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We denote
<math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1}(\mathbf{X})=\mathbf{W}_{o}^{h}\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1}(\mathbf{X})=\mathbf{W}_{o}^{h}\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{2}(\mathbf{X})=\sigma(\frac{(\mathbf{X})^{T}\mathbf{W}_{q}^{h}\mathbf{z}}{\sqrt{m}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{2}(\mathbf{X})=\sigma(\frac{(\mathbf{X})^{T}\mathbf{W}_{q}^{h}\mathbf{z}}{\sqrt{m}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, the difference in the output of the attention layer due to changes in <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{k}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{k}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{v}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{v}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\tau(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{E};\mathbf{\tilde{W}}_{k}^{h},\mathbf{\tilde{W}}_{v}^{h})-\tau(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{E};\mathbf{W}_{k}^{h},\mathbf{W}_{v}^{h})\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐄</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐄</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\tau(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{E};\mathbf{\tilde{W}}_{k}^{h},\mathbf{\tilde{W}}_{v}^{h})-\tau(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{E};\mathbf{W}_{k}^{h},\mathbf{W}_{v}^{h})\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{=\|\sum_{h=1}^{H}f_{1}(\mathbf{\tilde{W}}_{v}^{h}\mathbf{E})f_{2}(\mathbf{\tilde{W}}_{k}^{h}\mathbf{E})-\sum_{h=1}^{H}f_{1}(\mathbf{W}_{v}^{h}\mathbf{E})f_{2}(\mathbf{W}_{k}^{h}\mathbf{E})\|_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐄</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐄</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐄</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐄</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{=\|\sum_{h=1}^{H}f_{1}(\mathbf{\tilde{W}}_{v}^{h}\mathbf{E})f_{2}(\mathbf{\tilde{W}}_{k}^{h}\mathbf{E})-\sum_{h=1}^{H}f_{1}(\mathbf{W}_{v}^{h}\mathbf{E})f_{2}(\mathbf{W}_{k}^{h}\mathbf{E})\|_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\|f_{1}(\mathbf{\tilde{W}}_{v}^{h}\mathbf{E})f_{2}(\mathbf{\tilde{W}}_{k}^{h}\mathbf{E})-f_{1}(\mathbf{W}_{v}^{h}\mathbf{E})f_{2}(\mathbf{W}_{k}^{h}\mathbf{E})\|_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐄</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐄</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐄</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐄</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\leq\sum_{h=1}^{H}\|f_{1}(\mathbf{\tilde{W}}_{v}^{h}\mathbf{E})f_{2}(\mathbf{\tilde{W}}_{k}^{h}\mathbf{E})-f_{1}(\mathbf{W}_{v}^{h}\mathbf{E})f_{2}(\mathbf{W}_{k}^{h}\mathbf{E})\|_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
