<section id="A4.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.3.3 </span>Configurations of Explicit Contents Erasure</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For explicit contents erasure, we erased “nudity”, “naked”, “erotic” and “sexual” into “a person in modest clothing”. To erase implicit inappropriate concepts that can generate NSFW (Not Safer For Work) images through a diffusion model, we set a higher rank compared to celebrities erasure. The rank of the shared attention gate <math id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> was set to 64, and the rank <math id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> was set to 4. <math id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> for erasing loss was set to 3.0 and <math id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> for the attention anchoring loss was configured to <math id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0\times 10^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0\times 10^{4}</annotation></semantics></math>. To compute the attention anchoring loss, 240 sentences made by ChatGPT were used.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For training ResAG, we used Adam optimizer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kingma &amp; Ba, 2015</a>)</cite> with learning rate <math id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.0\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.0\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> for initial erasing stage and <math id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3.0\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.0\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> for the other erasing stages. For training the adversarial embeddings, we used Adam optimizer with learning rate <math id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math>. We scheduled the learning rate with cosine-with-restart for all cases <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Loshchilov &amp; Hutter, 2016</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We set 2400 iterations for initial erasing stage and 1200 iterations for subsequent erasing stages. For adversarial embeddings learning, 64 adversarial embeddings were trained for 1200 iterations for each stage. The training stage with erasing and adversarial embeddings learning was repeated across 20 times. The training time for each explicit concept took 1 hours on an A6000 GPU, Thus, erasing all 4 explicit concepts took about 4 A6000 GPU hours.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Additional Ablation Studies for CPE</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conducted studies on the performance variations in ResAG with respect to the rank <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{4}</annotation></semantics></math>, the value of <math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> in the erasing loss, and the value of <math id="A5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> in the attention anchoring loss. These studies were performed on celebrities erasure. Note that we set <math id="A5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to one for celebrities erasure, since the erasing effectiveness on target concepts and the preservation of remaining concepts were well maintained even with a rank of one. Table <a href="#A5.T1" title="Table E.1 ‣ Appendix E Additional Ablation Studies for CPE ‣ Concept Pinpoint Eraser for Text-to-image Diffusion Models via Residual Attention Gate" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a> shows the performance of CPE as the rank <math id="A5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> increases. We found that increasing the rank <math id="A5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> did not result in significant performance changes in both deletion and preservation. It highlights that the direction from target concepts to surrogate concepts lies in an extremely low-rank space.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table E.1: </span>Ablation study on the effect of rank <math id="A5.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The row with <span id="A5.T1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span> represents the selected configurations for comparison to baselines.</figcaption>
<div id="A5.T1.4" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:397.5pt;height:60.5pt;vertical-align:-28.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-163.9pt,24.9pt) scale(0.548118150357926,0.548118150357926) ;">
<table id="A5.T1.4.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
